 Each Character has a partially unique deck of 10 Action cards. To use one, discard that card face up **and** pay its cost by discarding the required number of additional Action cards. If a card has two sections separated by "OR," choose one.
 
+The original manual illustrates these card effects on page 13:
+
+| Action card | Extra Action-card cost | Effect |
+|---|---|---|
+| Captain's Basic Repairs | 2; Out of Combat only | Remove the Malfunction marker from your Room OR Repair/Break the Engine in your current Engine Room. |
+| Captain's Suppressive Fire | 0; In Combat only | **Discard 1 Ammo**, then move **yourself OR 1 other Character in your Room**, with that player's agreement, to a neighboring Room. This movement **does not trigger an Intruder Attack**. It moves one selected Character, not both. |
+| Pilot's Knowledge of the Ship | 0 | Open or Close 1 Door in a Corridor connected to your Room OR privately check 1 unexplored Room tile and return it face down, **without looking at its Exploration token**. |
+| Soldier's Full Auto | 0; In Combat only | Discard all Ammo from your **Assault Rifle** and perform a Shoot Action; the Ammo discarded determines the additional Injuries as clarified under the FAQ below. |
+
 ### Actions from Item cards
 
 Some Items grant Actions, described on their cards; discard the required number of Action cards to perform them. "One Use Only" Items are discarded after use.
